    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46401" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζώγρᾰφ-ος</span></b> , ὁ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωός</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωή, γράφω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who paints from life</i> or <i>from nature</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.46
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				448c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				453c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				656e
			</span></i>, etc.: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολιτειῶν ζ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					501c
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>painter</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Herod.</u>
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				41
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωγρ-</span> without iota, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				4.346
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				407
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				682.3
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, Pap. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Abh.Berl.Akad.</u>
				1904(2).6
			</span></i><span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				412.53
			</span></i>: so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωγραφία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					960.13
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.166S.
			</span></i>)</div>
